1
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:01,800
Hello everyone

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,100
Before we know it, it's exam season again

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,270
Recently, announcements for various provincial exams have been coming out one after another

4
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:09,830
In a sense

5
00:00:09,830 --> 00:00:12,650
I think the provincial exams might be even more important than the national ones

6
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,630
Because there are more diverse positions to choose from

7
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:17,320
And the general positions are usually quite good

8
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,720
But at the same time, it can be overwhelming

9
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,270
There are just so many

10
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:24,290
Choosing a position is a science.

11
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:30,220
It's also a headache for many people, especially new candidates.

12
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,060
The same few positions can be chosen from,

13
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:34,920
but the final admission scores can vary greatly.

14
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:38,070
And while it's not entirely accurate to say,

15
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:39,630
one exam determines your entire life,

16
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:44,820
getting out or changing once you're in can come at a significant cost,

17
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:48,600
which isn't something everyone can easily afford.

18
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,600
The purpose of making this video is

19
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,820
I hope everyone can have a clearer understanding before choosing a position.

20
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,480
Be more cautious.

21
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:57,520
Don’t be hasty.

22
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:00,980
And don’t think about just getting in first and figuring things out later.

23
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,780
Regarding the issue of position selection,

24
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:09,480
we must be clear about what we are actually selecting.

25
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:11,060
At the most basic level,

26
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:14,919
it’s crucial to first select positions that meet the criteria.

27
00:01:14,919 --> 00:01:17,479
Especially in Guangdong, where there’s no provincial manual intervention.

28
00:01:17,479 --> 00:01:19,919
It's crucial to be accountable to yourself

29
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,980
The first issue is the duration of grassroots work experience

30
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:27,640
Some positions, especially in provincial-level units

31
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,710
typically have such requirements

32
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:32,110
In the past, many people upon seeing this

33
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:35,570
assumed grassroots work definitely meant going to the countryside or something

34
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:37,310
thinking that working in private enterprises

35
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:38,360
didn't count for anything

36
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:42,030
Now, people probably wouldn't think that way anymore

37
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,230
His grassroots work experience

38
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:46,570
falls into several categories

39
00:01:46,570 --> 00:01:48,590
There are some special cases I haven't listed

40
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:49,990
but they don't affect many people

41
00:01:49,990 --> 00:01:51,525
so it doesn't matter

42
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:53,920
We need to categorize them

43
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,770
In this case

44
00:02:02,770 --> 00:02:06,930
it requires the district or county level, or the town level

45
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,160
if it's a municipality directly under the central government

46
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:13,140
The districts of a municipality are equivalent to cities in other regions.

47
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,980
But it still counts as grassroots work experience.

48
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:21,660
Of course, there is a special case here.

49
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:25,320
For example, if you work in a municipal-level government agency,

50
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,940
but your position is outside the official establishment,

51
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:28,810
What should we do then?

52
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,730
Some provinces explicitly state that

53
00:02:31,730 --> 00:02:33,910
it does count as work experience.

54
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:36,210
Provinces like Hunan, Anhui, and Ningxia, among others.

55
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:37,050
He mentioned it.

56
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:38,330
Whether it's the labor dispatch,

57
00:02:38,330 --> 00:02:43,290
or the hired personnel who are not on the regular payroll, they are included.

58
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:45,490
But some may not have been clear about it.

59
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:47,470
For instance, it seems that Guangdong didn't clarify this.

60
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:49,520
But I think they should all be included.

61
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,460
You can't say that because you're not on the regular payroll,

62
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:53,500
you should have the same treatment as those who are.

63
00:02:56,890 --> 00:03:03,250
I think he only restricted civil servants and those in similar positions.

64
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:05,010
Why is there such a rule?

65
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:05,570
Logically speaking,

66
00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:08,170
civil servants are not allowed to take the civil service exam, right?

67
00:03:08,170 --> 00:03:09,770
This is the case in most provinces.

68
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:14,540
But in the early days, it was allowed.

69
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:16,520
So they have continued this regulation ever since.

70
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:22,970
And indeed, there have been cases of former civil servants who once worked in provincial or municipal agencies,

71
00:03:22,970 --> 00:03:25,310
who resigned and later wanted to retake the exam.

72
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:28,370
Such situations do exist.

73
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:32,620
But most people actually don't need to pay much attention to this point.

74
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:36,060
And this village organization,

75
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,300
like the Village Committee,

76
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,530
is actually quite small, right?

77
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:41,090
Of course, regardless of that,

78
00:03:41,090 --> 00:03:45,270
everyone should understand that it is a grassroots work experience.

79
00:03:45,710 --> 00:03:50,050
Additionally, there are various enterprises and institutions here,

80
00:03:50,050 --> 00:03:53,910
whether they are state-owned or private companies,

81
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:56,920
or public sector positions.

82
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,640
You don’t need to worry about the hierarchy.

83
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:02,420
As long as you work in these places, it’s all good.

84
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:06,020
Whether you’re in a provincial or municipal public institution, it’s fine.

85
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:12,810
Regarding the work experience here,

86
00:04:12,810 --> 00:04:14,070
it doesn’t have to be consecutive.

87
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:16,329
As long as it adds up to two years, that’s fine.

88
00:04:16,329 --> 00:04:17,709
Make sure you do the math yourself.

89
00:04:17,709 --> 00:04:19,720
Calculate it month by month.

90
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,160
Try not to be too rigid about it.

91
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:24,060
If you just count it as 24 months,

92
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:26,220
there might be some risks involved.

93
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:28,260
I remember that in some places,

94
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:32,890
for example, if you started working on October 1, 2022, right?

95
00:04:32,890 --> 00:04:36,050
and it goes to September 30, 2024,

96
00:04:36,050 --> 00:04:37,410
it actually doesn’t count as two full years.

97
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:39,770
It only counts after October.

98
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:43,870
So, different places might have different details.

99
00:04:43,870 --> 00:04:46,470
Try not to be too rigid about it.

100
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:49,050
If you've just hit the 24-month mark,

101
00:04:49,050 --> 00:04:51,710
you might want to confirm with your workplace,

102
00:04:51,710 --> 00:04:53,070
just to be safe.

103
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:57,500
Also, I remember in Anhui,

104
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:03,540
the cut-off date for calculation is around July,

105
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:06,250
while other places use the day of registration.

106
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:07,810
Anhui is a bit different in this regard.

107
00:05:07,810 --> 00:05:10,910
Even though you currently only have one and a half years,

108
00:05:10,910 --> 00:05:13,770
by July, it will be two years.

109
00:05:13,770 --> 00:05:15,030
That works.

110
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:17,110
But you need to make sure you don't lose your job in between.

111
00:05:17,110 --> 00:05:20,810
If you become unemployed, it won't be continuous.

112
00:05:20,810 --> 00:05:22,130
It won't continue seamlessly.

113
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:23,810
In other words, it won't accumulate.

114
00:05:23,810 --> 00:05:26,000
It might not be enough.

115
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:33,810
And then there's the documentation to support it.

116
00:05:33,810 --> 00:05:36,110
Generally speaking, they put it this way.

117
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:37,290
Provide your employment contract.

118
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:38,890
proof of income or social security

119
00:05:38,890 --> 00:05:41,410
though it seems to be about the goods relationship

120
00:05:41,410 --> 00:05:45,490
but in fact, in the actual qualification review

121
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:48,530
the supporting documents are definitely better when more comprehensive

122
00:05:48,530 --> 00:05:51,370
the most important thing here is social security

123
00:05:53,050 --> 00:05:54,010
why is social security so crucial

124
00:05:54,010 --> 00:05:57,030
because it’s hard to forge social security

125
00:05:58,550 --> 00:06:01,790
while the other items

126
00:06:01,790 --> 00:06:04,770
might have some potential for human manipulation

127
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:06,730
So employers might avoid risks

128
00:06:06,730 --> 00:06:09,280
by not providing social insurance

129
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:12,440
and thus not approving your application

130
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,940
If you haven’t paid social insurance

131
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:18,420
for this job

132
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:22,250
the company simply doesn’t contribute to your social insurance

133
00:06:23,170 --> 00:06:27,420
this indeed poses significant risks in terms of recognition

134
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:30,940
Additionally, if the duration of social insurance contributions doesn’t match the contract

135
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:34,410
for example, if you’ve been contributing for one year and nine months

136
00:06:34,410 --> 00:06:36,470
Then the contract is for ten months of a year.

137
00:06:36,470 --> 00:06:39,950
In this case, it's highly likely that he will base it on the social security timeline.

138
00:06:39,950 --> 00:06:41,770
That is, it will be recognized as nine months of a year.

139
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:46,760
But this isn't certain; it's just a possibility.

140
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:52,480
If you can't ensure you'll have enough supporting documents,

141
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,169
I suggest you don't take the risk.

142
00:06:54,169 --> 00:06:55,689
When I was in Xiamen before,

143
00:06:55,689 --> 00:06:58,369
I had a friend who was in charge of this area at the Intermediate Court,

144
00:06:58,369 --> 00:07:01,990
At that time, there was a candidate applying for their organization.

145
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:03,990
Although his piecemeal experience adds up

146
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:05,710
to exactly 24 months

147
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:09,980
there was a small section of the supporting documents that had issues

148
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:12,480
which ultimately led to the recognized experience

149
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,680
being only one year and ten months

150
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,940
which is less than two years

151
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:18,320
and thus he wasn't eligible for the position

152
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,460
which is really unfortunate

153
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:23,680
I remember this issue was discovered during the political review stage

154
00:07:55,370 --> 00:07:57,180
It's fine as long as you haven't secured a job.

155
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,300
Does it matter what happened before?

156
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,750
It's generally like this in Guangdong.

157
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:07,350
Anyway, I've seen many cities clearly state this.

158
00:08:07,350 --> 00:08:08,350
This situation is acceptable.

159
00:08:08,350 --> 00:08:14,700
But, the interpretation might vary from city to city.

160
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:19,730
So, it's best to confirm with your employer.

161
00:08:20,010 --> 00:08:22,690
However, in a case like Guangdong's,

162
00:08:22,690 --> 00:08:25,610
It means that it's okay if you don't have a job when you apply.

163
00:08:25,610 --> 00:08:28,409
You’d better not apply and then look for a job afterward.

164
00:08:28,409 --> 00:08:31,889
Otherwise, it’s hard to say how they will evaluate your situation.

165
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:36,039
You should state that you don’t have a job when you apply.

166
00:08:36,039 --> 00:08:38,299
It’s best to maintain this status.

167
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:41,299
If you want to, huh.

168
00:08:41,299 --> 00:08:43,159
Next, let’s talk about the form of study.

169
00:08:43,159 --> 00:08:45,300
That is, the issue of full-time education.

170
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:47,560
There used to be a common misconception.

171
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:50,780
That civil service exams require a full-time education degree.

172
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,800
You can only apply for correspondence courses and such.

173
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,240
This adult education doesn't count.

174
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,880
Even now, some people still say that.

175
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:59,950
Most positions have restrictions on full-time education.

176
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:04,150
In fact, there are specific requirements for full-time education.

177
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:07,540
That is, the requirements set by regular higher education institutions.

178
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:10,490
Basically, only courts and procuratorates.

179
00:09:10,490 --> 00:09:13,530
Other organizations only impose such restrictions on recent graduates.

180
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:15,850
Only then does it essentially equate to a full-time education requirement.

181
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:18,520
Because it's only for fresh graduates

182
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:21,450
It's only the full-time programs that have the fresh graduate status

183
00:09:21,450 --> 00:09:23,610
Otherwise, you won't see other organizations

184
00:09:23,610 --> 00:09:25,430
It doesn't limit to fresh graduates

185
00:09:25,430 --> 00:09:26,849
But it does restrict to full-time students

186
00:09:26,849 --> 00:09:28,469
I've never seen that, anyway

187
00:09:28,469 --> 00:09:29,889
Or other types of organizations

188
00:09:29,889 --> 00:09:31,969
Or they are extremely rare

189
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,300
Especially in some remote areas

190
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:38,980
It might not even require full-time study for the legal examination.

191
00:09:39,549 --> 00:09:42,509
You'll see that phrase in almost all of their announcements.

192
00:09:44,189 --> 00:09:46,890
So if you're in a tough major,

193
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:50,839
feel free to pursue a good adult education program.

194
00:09:51,079 --> 00:09:54,039
The only thing is, you can't take the legal examination or apply for fresh graduate positions.

195
00:09:54,039 --> 00:09:55,700
But you can apply for everything else.

196
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:57,380
And here it also mentions,

197
00:09:57,380 --> 00:10:00,400
the part-time graduate students and full-time graduate students,

198
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:02,960
have equal eligibility for application.

199
00:10:07,489 --> 00:10:10,789
Then, in the announcement for the public examination,

200
00:10:10,789 --> 00:10:12,309
this phrase also appears.

201
00:10:12,309 --> 00:10:15,109
But what exactly are the eligibility requirements?

202
00:10:15,109 --> 00:10:18,629
Can he still be considered a recent graduate?

203
00:10:18,629 --> 00:10:21,629
This seems to vary by province.

204
00:10:21,629 --> 00:10:22,389
Currently,

205
00:10:22,389 --> 00:10:27,590
most of them do not recognize part-time graduate students as recent graduates.

206
00:10:27,590 --> 00:10:29,790
Gradually, it appears that some are starting to recognize them.

207
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:34,660
This also needs to be analyzed on a case-by-case basis.

208
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:39,960
Speaking of this, there's a special point to mention.

209
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,140
It's about the household registration requirements in Guangdong Province.

210
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,640
I'm sure many people have noticed this.

211
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:48,190
Guangdong Province mentions that for those with household registration from other provinces,

212
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:49,190
if they want to apply to Guangdong Province,

213
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:53,670
they should have a full-time education status.

214
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:57,820
There's one scenario where if someone has household registration from another province,

215
00:10:57,820 --> 00:11:00,420
they themselves have full-time education rights,

216
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:03,740
but they also have other adult education qualifications.

217
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:05,060
For example, self-study exams and the like

218
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:07,630
He wants to use this to register for exams

219
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:08,790
But is it actually feasible?

220
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:12,950
Let me share my personal view

221
00:11:12,950 --> 00:11:15,650
From a literal interpretation, it seems viable

222
00:11:15,650 --> 00:11:18,740
Because the announcement restricts the identity of the applicants

223
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,740
Not the nature of their educational qualifications

224
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:22,700
If they intended to restrict the educational qualifications

225
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:27,390
They should have specified non-Guangdong household registration

226
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:33,570
Applicants must have a full-time academic degree or above.

227
00:11:33,570 --> 00:11:34,330
Full-time

228
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:39,270
Or a bachelor's degree or above from a regular higher education institution.

229
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:46,339
This is the accurate way to describe the educational qualification requirements.

230
00:11:46,339 --> 00:11:48,579
But now it restricts the identity of the applicants.

231
00:11:48,579 --> 00:11:49,999
Why do I think so?

232
00:11:49,999 --> 00:11:51,979
One reason is the wording itself.

233
00:11:51,979 --> 00:11:55,430
And the beginning of this regulation states,

234
00:11:55,430 --> 00:12:00,910
It's fundamentally about the level of education, right?

235
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:03,090
Cultural level is inherently a human attribute

236
00:12:03,090 --> 00:12:06,370
rather than a specific educational qualification

237
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,520
like the Shenzhen civil service examination

238
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,840
is quite clear on this point

239
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:13,260
the guidelines not only include

240
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:14,820
a statement similar to that of the Guangdong provincial exam

241
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:16,620
but also specifically add

242
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:20,380
that individuals who have both full-time and adult education qualifications

243
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:23,480
can choose to apply using either one

244
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:26,320
The provincial exam, however, just lacks clear guidelines

245
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:28,130
rather than being outright rejected

246
00:12:28,130 --> 00:12:30,830
Shenzhen also participates in the provincial exam, right?

247
00:12:30,830 --> 00:12:35,170
It's highly unlikely that there would be two different review processes

248
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:38,210
Let's compare this with the regulations for the Jiangsu provincial exam

249
00:12:38,210 --> 00:12:40,130
In the announcement for Suzhou

250
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:42,060
it states that

251
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:47,759
obtaining a master’s degree or higher

252
00:12:47,759 --> 00:12:51,999
and then applying as a social candidate with a postgraduate degree

253
00:12:51,999 --> 00:12:54,500
Not restricted by household registration

254
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:57,180
This is a rigorous way of expression

255
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:59,180
Although he is not talking about full-time education issues

256
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:01,180
But we can make an analogy

257
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:06,180
If he wants to restrict the majors for application

258
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:10,540
He would clearly specify the conditions for application

259
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:14,850
In Suzhou, he mentioned applying with a master's degree

260
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:16,620
Similarly, in Guangdong

261
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:17,740
